        <h2>Summary / Description</h2>
        <div class="description">
          To maximize benefits from the data sent to the ground by the Lower Body Negative Pressure (LBNP) Controller and the Data Acquisition System, a new system was developed for data acquisition from the Shuttle downlink telemetry. The Operations Acquisition System In-situ (OASIS) is a portable, ground-based data processing system used to decode, display, and store information received from the Space Shuttle telemetry stream during LBNP operations in the middeck or the Spacelab. The OASIS can be used anywhere that access to telemetry data is available, such as the Science Monitoring Area (SMA) at JSC, the Payload Operations Control Centers (POCC) at MSFC and JSC, or during preflight testing in the Operations and Checkout Building at KSC. 
<P>
The OASIS has a custom-designed Dual Serial Receiver board, together with special data acquisition cards in a personal computer (PC) system running customized software (developed under a LabViews platform). The OASIS system utilizes two PCs (laptops with expansion chassis or desktops) to perform all of the functions that have previously required two racks of electronic equipment, a MicroVAX computer and a network of Macintosh workstations. Virtual instrumentation displays on the PC monitors can be customized to perform data analysis in real or near-real time.  Selected information can be displayed to investigators and medical personnel monitoring the experiment (blood pressure and heart rate trend analysis, pulse pressure monitoring, power spectral analysis of electrocardiograms, etc.). Alarms can be programmed to alert when heart rate or blood pressure approaches predetermined test termination criteria. The multitasking capabilities of the PC workstations are optimized to display data in multiple windows simultaneously.<end>
        </div>

